238
00:11:02,529 --> 00:11:03,396
I know

239
00:11:03,396 --> 00:11:05,131
Just the right amount is best

240
00:11:09,869 --> 00:11:11,404
It's time for today's

241
00:11:11,404 --> 00:11:13,206
Food Facts!

242
00:11:17,677 --> 00:11:19,279
Pigs have both large and small intestines

243
00:11:19,279 --> 00:11:20,947
Stuff glutinous rice into a pig's large intestine

244
00:11:20,947 --> 00:11:22,749
and you can make a rice sausage

245
00:11:22,749 --> 00:11:23,750
Got it!

246
00:11:24,350 --> 00:11:26,219
If you stuff meat into a pig's small intestine,

247
00:11:26,219 --> 00:11:28,354
you can make the sausages we often eat

248
00:11:29,222 --> 00:11:30,223
Cool!

249
00:11:30,957 --> 00:11:32,892
I want to learn more!

250
00:11:32,892 --> 00:11:33,693
No problem!

251
00:11:34,694 --> 00:11:36,095
Wrap a sausage in a rice sausage

252
00:11:36,095 --> 00:11:37,630
and you get Big Sausage Wraps Little Sausage

253
00:11:37,630 --> 00:11:39,365
It's a special Taiwanese snack

254
00:11:39,365 --> 00:11:40,567
People from other countries think it's cool too

255
00:11:41,701 --> 00:11:42,569
And all around the world,

256
00:11:42,569 --> 00:11:44,571
there are dishes made by stuffing meat into casings

257
00:11:44,571 --> 00:11:45,772
such as German sausages,

258
00:11:45,772 --> 00:11:47,507
French blood sausage, and Italian salami

259
00:11:49,175 --> 00:11:51,444
I love delicious food!

260
00:11:58,651 --> 00:12:00,653
